            "review_title": "Review at Grounded Chay - 75 Nhị Hà",
            "review_text": "Happy Travels\nChino Hills, California89 contributions\n1\nReal vegan food, and good portion sizes.\nFeb 2024 • Couples\nGROUNDED CHAY VEGAN RESTAURANT Nha Trang: (aka, \"Grounded - Toast Coffee Vegetarian\" on Google maps)\nA great small Mostly-Vegan restaurant, in Nha Trang. Just give the Google Map reference to your taxi driver or Grab driver. This restaurant serves real vegan food, and has good portion sizes. (maybe only 2 dishes on the menu have egg). The owners are super nice and can tell you about how they make the dishes, and they really care about hearing customer feedback. This place is clean and quirky, and a lot of effort has gone into it. This restaurant is something special and totally worth supporting. We ate the grounded vegan Tofu Burger, and the vegan Dumplings that were the best we have had in all of Vietnam. I wish that there were more places like this, but this is a unique gem.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nSearch for \"Grounded - Toast Coffee Vegetarian\" on Google maps.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten March 5, 2024",
